    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, the \"small moments\" feel so hollow when you look at the bigger picture. like, what's the point of finding \"purpose\" in a world that's just going to burn or drown anyway? it's like being told to enjoy the view while you're in a house that's actively on fire. it feels like we're just delaying the inevitable, and it's exhausting to keep pretending that any of this matters. doesn't it just feel... illogical to keep fighting for a future that isn't actually coming?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
